<.shell title="Messages" current={:feedback}>
  <h1>Messages</h1>
  <p class="lead">Tell people what happened, what's important, and what to do next.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Toast</strong>: the result of what the person did. It comes and goes.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Banner</strong>: something true about the page until it changes. It stays.</li>
    <li><strong>Error summary</strong>: what to fix in a form after a failed save.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Toasts</h2>
  <p>
    LiveView's flash messages. One card per message, stacked at the top right on a desktop and at
    the bottom on a phone, where a thumb can close it.
  </p>
  <div class="demo">
    <div class="toasts">
      <.flash id="sample-flash-info" kind={:info}>4 attendance changes saved to D4H.</.flash>
      <.flash id="sample-flash-error" kind={:error} title="D4H did not accept the change">
        Nothing changed. Check the D4H access key in team settings.
      </.flash>
      <.flash id="sample-flash-disconnected" kind={:error} title="Server disconnected">
        Reconnecting… <.icon name="hero-arrow-path" class="ml-1 h-3 w-3 animate-spin" />
      </.flash>
    </div>
  </div>
  <.form_actions>
    <.button data-toast="info">Show an info toast</.button>
    <.button data-toast="error">Show an error toast</.button>
  </.form_actions>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Info toasts are for success and progress. Error toasts get a short title, then what to do.
    </li>
    <li>
      The Server disconnected toast shows while LiveView reconnects and goes when it is back.
    </li>
    <li>Never put the only copy of important information in a toast. Use a banner.</li>
    <li>
      In the app: <code>put_flash(socket, :info, "…")</code>. The layout's
      <code>&lt;.flash_group&gt;</code>
      shows them with <code>&lt;.flash&gt;</code>.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <div class="toasts" id="toasts" aria-live="polite"></div>
  <template id="toast-info">
    <.flash id="sample-toast-info" kind={:info}>Settings saved.</.flash>
  </template>
  <template id="toast-error">
    <.flash id="sample-toast-error" kind={:error} title="Letter not created">
      Enter who authorizes tax letters in team settings.
    </.flash>
  </template>
  <script>
    document.querySelectorAll("[data-toast]").forEach(function (button) {
      button.addEventListener("click", function () {
        var kind = button.dataset.toast;
        var toast = document.getElementById("toast-" + kind).content.firstElementChild.cloneNode(true);
        toast.removeAttribute("id");
        document.getElementById("toasts").appendChild(toast);
        toast.addEventListener("click", function () { toast.remove(); });
        if (kind !== "error") setTimeout(function () { toast.remove(); }, 5000);
      });
    });
  </script>

  <h2>Confirm dialog</h2>
  <p>
    Before a change that cannot be undone. The question names the thing and says what happens.
  </p>
  <div class="demo">
    <.button
      variant={:danger}
      data-confirm="Delete the First Aid clause? Its 3 qualifications are removed from the group rule."
    >
      Delete clause
    </.button>
  </div>
  <p class="spec">
    In the app: <code>data-confirm="…"</code>
    on the button. The browser shows its own dialog, with OK and Cancel.
  </p>
  <div class="demo">
    <div class="dialog" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="confirm-title-static">
      <h2 id="confirm-title-static">Delete the First Aid clause?</h2>
      <p class="paragraph">
        Its 3 qualifications are removed from the group rule. Members stay in the group until you apply the rule.
      </p>
      <.form_actions>
        <.button variant={:danger}>Delete clause</.button>
        <.button>Cancel</.button>
      </.form_actions>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="spec not-yet">
    Not used in the app yet: a <code>.dialog</code>
    whose buttons say what happens. Today every confirm is the browser's.
  </p>
  <script>
    document.querySelectorAll("[data-confirm]").forEach(function (button) {
      button.addEventListener("click", function () { window.confirm(button.dataset.confirm); });
    });
  </script>

  <h2>Banners</h2>
  <p>At the top of the page, under the header. One at a time.</p>
  <div class="example">
    <div class="banner banner-success" role="status">
      <div class="banner-title">
        <.icon name="hero-check-circle-mini" class="size-5" />Success
      </div>
      <div class="banner-body">
        <p><strong>12 tax credit letters created for 2025.</strong></p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="banner" role="region" aria-label="Important">
      <div class="banner-title">
        <.icon name="hero-information-circle-mini" class="size-5" />Important
      </div>
      <div class="banner-body">
        <p>
          SAR Duty refreshes from D4H every night at 02:00. Changes made in D4H today show up tomorrow.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="banner banner-warning" role="region" aria-label="Warning">
      <div class="banner-title">
        <.icon name="hero-exclamation-triangle-mini" class="size-5" />Warning
      </div>
      <div class="banner-body">
        <p>
          The team's D4H access key belongs to a person. If they leave the team, it stops working.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="banner banner-danger" role="alert">
      <div class="banner-title">
        <.icon name="hero-exclamation-circle-mini" class="size-5" />D4H is not answering
      </div>
      <div class="banner-body">
        <p>Nothing changed. Try again in a few minutes.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="spec">
    In the app: <code>.banner</code>, with <code>.banner-success</code>, <code>.banner-warning</code>, or <code>.banner-danger</code>, and a
    <code>.banner-title</code>
    and <code>.banner-body</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>Error summary</h2>
  <p>
    At the top of a form after a failed save, linking to each field. See <a href={
      page_path(:forms)
    }>Forms</a>.
  </p>
  <div class="example">
    <div class="error-summary" role="alert">
      <h2>There is a problem</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="#">Enter who authorizes tax letters</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="spec not-yet">
    Not used in the app yet: forms show each error on its field.
  </p>

  <h2>Warning text</h2>
  <div class="example">
    <div class="warning-text">
      <.icon name="hero-exclamation-triangle" class="size-6" />
      <span>Attendance cannot be changed once the activity is published in D4H.</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="spec">For a consequence people must know before they act.</p>

  <h2>Inset text</h2>
  <div class="example">
    <div class="inset">
      Members are matched by name, email, or phone. You review every change before it's made.
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="spec">For a note that helps, set apart from the main text.</p>
  <p class="spec not-yet">Not used in the app yet.</p>

  <h2>Callout</h2>
  <div class="example">
    <div class="callout">
      Use the president's full name and title. CRA reads it in an audit.
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="spec">Advice beside a form field, such as on the team settings page.</p>

  <h2>Empty state</h2>
  <div class="example">
    <div class="empty-state">
      <strong>No tax credit letters for 2025 yet</strong>
      <p>Letters are made from attendance in D4H. Create one from the member list.</p>
      <.button size={:sm} href="#">Go to tax credit letters</.button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="spec">Say why it's empty and what to do, not only "No results".</p>
  <p class="spec not-yet">Not used in the app yet: empty lists say so in a line of text.</p>

  <h2>Loading</h2>
  <div class="demo">
    <p class="paragraph">
      <.spinner>Refreshing from D4H…</.spinner>
    </p>
    <p class="text-sm text-secondary-1">
      <.spinner>Calculating driving distances for 14 members…</.spinner>
    </p>
  </div>
  <p class="spec">
    Name the slow thing. Spinners slow down when the system asks for reduced motion. In the app: <code>&lt;.spinner&gt;Refreshing from D4H…&lt;/.spinner&gt;</code>.
  </p>
</.shell>
